{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789257273,"nonce":"36UDfLQ0zFZARWiGXMPFgjgLSas=","title":"Cranelift main path refuses IncRef, DecRef and Drop","message":"Since ee2a3ce the main body-compilation path errors on any intrinsic it\ndoes not list instead of skipping it, and it never listed IncRef, DecRef\nor Drop; only the older translate_instruction path lowers them. The ARC\nmemory strategy (the CompilerConfig default) emits all three, so a\nfunction carrying one fails to compile. Surfaced by\ncranelift_backend_tests::test_memory_management_intrinsics, which the\nlib-only test runs after ee2a3ce did not cover.\n\nFix: lower them on the main path as translate_instruction does (count\nin the first word, free at zero, drop as a no-op until destructor\ndispatch exists), through a helper that borrows only the JIT module\nbecause the builder holds the codegen context.","files":null}]}